# Pairs with EveryCommittedKeyReadable. The commit fan-out declares the saga
# done once ANY participant has applied the commit terminal, so the rest are
# never told and never materialise the committed value. Every invariant still
# holds: the gate serves a skipped key's prepared value post-saga for as long
# as the registry reports the commit, so no reader ever sees a split view or a
# pre-saga value. That is what makes this the pairing that shows the property
# is not entailed by an invariant: with this mutation,
# ([]VisibilityMatchesDecision /\ []AllOrNothing) => EveryCommittedKeyReadable
# is violated. (The pairing this replaced, a projection that switched on an
# abort terminal, also broke VisibilityMatchesDecision and AllOrNothing, so it
# could not show that.)
#
# It fires NoStrandedPrepare too, and cannot avoid doing so: in this model a
# committed key materialises exactly when its terminal lands. Only committed
# sagas are affected, so Termination stays green.
MODULE: EveryCommittedKeyReadableCommitFanOutStops
TARGET: EveryCommittedKeyReadable
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the commit fan-out stops after its first participant, so a committed key is never materialised although every read is consistent
PERTURBS: BroadcastStep

--- FIND
           allDone == \A j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: on the commit path "some participant applied its terminal" is
\* mistaken for "every participant did". Compensation is unchanged.
           allDone == IF phase[t] = "committing"
                      THEN \E j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
                      ELSE \A j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
--- END